{% comment %}
  blocks/spacer.liquid

  Vertical space.

  An escape hatch, and a deliberate one. Merchants need a gap the section's own
  padding does not give them, and the alternative is an empty text block with
  three line breaks in it — which is worse markup, worse for screen readers, and
  harder to remove later.

  Hidden from assistive technology: it is a gap, not content.
{% endcomment %}

<div
  class="block-spacer
    {%- if block.settings.show_divider %} block-spacer--divider{% endif -%}
    {%- if block.settings.divider_mobile_only %} block-spacer--divider-mobile{% endif -%}"
  style="--spacer-height: {{ block.settings.height }}px; --spacer-height-mobile: {{ block.settings.height_mobile | default: block.settings.height }}px;"
  aria-hidden="true"
  {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
></div>

{% comment %}
  The divider is drawn on the spacer itself rather than as a separate block,
  because a rule and the space around it are one decision. Two blocks would let a
  merchant end up with a line and no room around it.
{% endcomment %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:blocks.spacer.name",
  "tag": null,
  "settings": [
    { "type": "range", "id": "height", "label": "t:blocks.spacer.settings.height.label", "min": 4, "max": 160, "step": 4, "unit": "px", "default": 32 },
    { "type": "range", "id": "height_mobile", "label": "t:blocks.spacer.settings.height_mobile.label", "min": 0, "max": 120, "step": 4, "unit": "px", "default": 0 }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "t:blocks.spacer.name" }]
}
{% endschema %}
